            "review_title": "Review at River View Restaurant And Coffee",
            "review_text": "George M\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam26 contributions\n1\nStaff training needs to be a priority\nFeb 2019 • Friends\nMyself, a friend and his wife went to the River View after she had found it on the internet and everything we read looked great.\nWhen we arrived, we were met by a middle eastern gentleman, who asked if we wanted to sit on the sidewalk, inside or inside upstairs. As there was a pleasant breeze we chose the sidewalk, where we could also enjoy the view. He seated us and wished us a good evening, and went to sit with friends.\nA Vietnamese waiter then arrived with two menus, and did not respond to being asked to bring a third. When asked if they served beer, he said yes, but they only have Heineken, so we asked for three, while we decided on food. He arrived with three warm Tiger beers, which he then promptly dropped and spread across the sidewalk. He took these away and then returned with cold Heinekens.\nWe then ordered seafood spring rolls and chicken wings, to share as starters. Shortly after that another young waiter approached and asked my friends Vietnamese wife, if we had ordered spring rolls, when she replied to the positive, he responded by saying we can only order what was on the menu. The lady then showed it to him on the menu and he rushed off.\nThe first guy the came back and insisted on taking our main course orders. \nThe food was tasty, but the lack of training of the serving staff, made the visit no more than average. I will give it another visit to check, but if the service does not improve, it will be the last.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nWritten March 1, 2019",
